(3, 7, FALSE, 10); -- Romantic Retreat
Sample Queries
To retrieve information about pubs based on different criteria, you can use queries like these:

Pubs with a high cosy-lively scale:
sql
Copy code
SELECT Pubs.name, Ratings.cosy_lively_scale
FROM Pubs
JOIN Ratings ON Pubs.pub_id = Ratings.pub_id
WHERE Ratings.cosy_lively_scale > 8;
Pubs where you can watch sports:
sql
Copy code
SELECT Pubs.name, Ratings.can_watch_sports
FROM Pubs
JOIN Ratings ON Pubs.pub_id = Ratings.pub_id
WHERE Ratings.can_watch_sports = TRUE;
Pubs with a high date night rating:
sql
Copy code
SELECT Pubs.name, Ratings.date_night_rating
FROM Pubs
JOIN Ratings ON Pubs.pub_id = Ratings.pub_id
WHERE Ratings.date_night_rating > 8;
All information about pubs:
sql
Copy code
SELECT Pubs.name, Pubs.address, Pubs.phone_number, 
       Ratings.cosy_lively_scale, Ratings.can_watch_sports, Ratings.date_night_rating
FROM Pubs
JOIN Ratings ON Pubs.pub_id = Ratings.pub_id;
This schema design allows you to effectively store and retrieve pub information based on the given criteria. You can further expand the database by adding more attributes or tables as needed.
